branch: feature/monoid-scope
worktree: ../okay-wt-mscope
spec: docs/di.md ("a collection is not special"), Fold.scala

why: the base Monoid instances live in two places and it shows.
  `vector` is in the companion — its own comment says "being here it
  needs no import" — while String, List and the Alternative family
  are top level in package okay. MEASURED from okay.deploy:
  `Fact[Vector[Int]]` resolves, `Fact[String]` does not without
  `import okay.given`. The docs sample `object Notes extends
  Fact[String]` is therefore wrong for a reader outside the library.

what: move Monoid[String] and Monoid[List[A]] into the companion
  beside `vector`; leave the Alternative-derived family top level (it
  is for F[_] families and would compete there). A test in okay-deploy
  proves both resolve OUTSIDE package okay, which is the property that
  was never pinned.

next: move, pin it from outside, check nothing became ambiguous
